<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95637" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοῦσον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lily</i>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρίνον</span>, Aristobulus and <i><span class="en">
				Chares
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				12.513f
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				838a23
			</span></i> (Phoen.and Phrygian word, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Zonar.
			</span></i>; cf. Hebr. <i>shûshan</i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σασά</span></b>  Syrian acc. to Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.102
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σοῦσα</span></b> , τά, <u>Susa</u>, in the province of Susiana or
			Shushan, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.188
			</span></i>; the winter and spring residence of the King of Persia,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.6.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.</u>
				3.5.15
			</span></i>:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σούσιος</span></b> , ὁ, <i>a man of
			Susa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.1.2
			</span></i>:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σουσίς</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ,
				<i>the province of Susa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				119
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				557
			</span></i> (s.v.l.) (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σ. γυνή</span> a woman
				<i>of Susa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.6.11
			</span></i>); also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σουσιάδες</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					17.68
				</span></i>
			; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σουσιανή</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.2
			</span></i>. (Derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοῦσον</span> acc.
			to <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοῦσαν</span> codd.).)</div>
